---
import Shell from "../../../layouts/Shell.astro";
import KingdomNav from "../../../components/kingdom/shared/KingdomNav.astro";
import MyRequirements from "../../../components/kingdom/my/MyRequirements";
import "../../../components/kingdom/shared/kingdom.css";
import "../../../components/kingdom/requirements/requirements.css";
import "../../../components/kingdom/my/my.css";
---
<Shell title="My requirements" description="Open your council's requirements card, enter your own numbers and see your KvK target, your DKP so far and what it takes to close the gap." mode="operate">
  <div class="kg">
    <header class="kg-head">
      <h1>My requirements</h1>
      <p class="kg-lead">Open the card your council published, enter your own numbers and see your target, your progress and what it takes to close the gap.</p>
    </header>
    <KingdomNav section="members" leaderOnly />
    <section class="km-explainer" aria-labelledby="km-what-h" data-explainer>
      <h2 id="km-what-h">What is DKP?</h2>
      <p>DKP isn't a game number: each kingdom sets its own formula, usually points for T4 and T5 kills plus more points for dead troops (fact B08-0001). Your council then asks for a DKP target, often as a percent of your power: "250% of power" means a 10.5M-power player needs 26.25M DKP. It is counted from what you gain between the start scan and the end scan, not your lifetime totals (fact B08-0002).</p>
    </section>
    <MyRequirements client:load />
  </div>
</Shell>
